      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Lightheadedness and nausea are common with severe migraines, so waiting it out with ibuprofen and sleep might be the right approach if you feel otherwise stable. However, since you are experiencing sudden, intense symptoms, it's wise to consider a little extra caution. If the headache doesn't start improving within a few hours, or if the lightheadedness worsens, it's probably best to have a medical professional check in.",
